{"title":"2025 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 8","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Diagram\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Diagram</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Note\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Note</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_Law_of_(Co)Sine\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 Law of (Co)Sine</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Ptolemy’s_+_Similarity)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Ptolemy’s + Similarity)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Area_&amp;_Angle_Bisector_Length)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Area &amp; Angle Bisector Length)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Power_Solve\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Power Solve</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(Cyclic_Quads_+_LoC)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (Cyclic Quads + LoC)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_4_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 4 by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Pentagon <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/3/f13a96240c51d61ba3733d9f5c3020fa92ec4136.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCDE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" /> is inscribed in a circle, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/0/e908ad82d6d453d2916d9fe85e730654b8f44571.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BEC = \\angle CED = 30^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"190\" height=\"15\" />. Let line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89fff82bb65d0215e49c8c91cb7c553da52205e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> intersect at point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/f/a9fe059ea3506a79afe2df3583a0b5e584fb92d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/6/ca6371efb1262af8539ffffcb75a931ef3fb43cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD = 24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" />. What is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/e/65e4f2d5cc59e5ffbed3734130e8c45b643adc91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/c/bbc4f1b09ec7d273aed7451f557f30466a202564.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } \\frac{57}{11} \\qquad\\textbf{(B) } \\frac{59}{11} \\qquad\\textbf{(C) } \\frac{60}{11} \\qquad\\textbf{(D) } \\frac{61}{11} \\qquad\\textbf{(E) } \\frac{63}{11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"421\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Diagram\">Diagram</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Diagram\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/c/a0c98eac90afb3e64254427b6b3b547deffa52d6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] /* Made by MRENTHUSIASM */ size(200); real r = 7*sqrt(3); pair O, A, B, C, D, E, F; O = origin; B = r*dir(30); C = r*dir(-30); D = r*dir(-90); E = r*dir(180); A = intersectionpoints(Circle(O,r),Circle(B,9))[0]; F = intersectionpoint(A--C,B--D);  draw(Circle(O,r)^^A--B--C--D--E--cycle^^D--B--E--C--A--cycle); dot(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,1.5*B/r,linewidth(4)); dot(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,1.5*C/r,linewidth(4)); dot(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,1.5*D/r,linewidth(4)); dot(&quot;$E$&quot;,E,1.5*E/r,linewidth(4)); dot(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,1.5*A/r,linewidth(4)); dot(&quot;$F$&quot;,F,1.5*F/r,linewidth(4)); label(&quot;$30^{\\circ}$&quot;,E,6*(1,0),fontsize(8)); label(&quot;$30^{\\circ}$&quot;,E,7*dir(-32),fontsize(8)); label(&quot;$9$&quot;,0.92*midpoint(A--B)); label(&quot;$24$&quot;,1.8*midpoint(A--D)); [/asy]\" width=\"325\" height=\"335\" />\n~MRENTHUSIASM\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We will scale down the diagram by a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/5/9055b2dbb0dbbb85db675f34efda18f16926ef68.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/0/0f06a04f48b3ffbd7958dba7ee749a176270aafc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD = 8.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"69\" height=\"14\" /> Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/5/975ea71eb98201730bde57fdb624e3ca12ee724b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BEC = 30^{\\circ},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"113\" height=\"18\" /> it follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/a/5aac5ae5e55c23b66c778969810fdea10dd18f05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAC = \\angle BDC = 30^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"189\" height=\"15\" /> as they all subtend the same arc. Similarly, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/8/5d8b591d64c50c7b288718c3e099b30733d8504e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CED = 30^{\\circ},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"114\" height=\"18\" /> it follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/6/d66a90e9c20fe3c0940d8ad35d390d304662f0dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CAD = \\angle CBD = 30^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"190\" height=\"15\" /> as well.\n</p><p>We obtain the following diagram:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/2/842cfd63a0c4f4dab18a67c7d94b9988da1d386c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] /* Made by MRENTHUSIASM */ size(200); real r = 7*sqrt(3); pair O, A, B, C, D, E, F; O = origin; B = r*dir(30); C = r*dir(-30); D = r*dir(-90); E = r*dir(180); A = intersectionpoints(Circle(O,r),Circle(B,9))[0]; F = intersectionpoint(A--C,B--D);  draw(Circle(O,r)^^B--C--D--E--A^^B--E--C--F); draw(A--D--B--cycle^^A--F,red); dot(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,1.5*B/r,linewidth(4)); dot(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,1.5*C/r,linewidth(4)); dot(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,1.5*D/r,linewidth(4)); dot(&quot;$E$&quot;,E,1.5*E/r,linewidth(4)); dot(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,1.5*A/r,linewidth(4)); dot(&quot;$F$&quot;,F,1.5*F/r,linewidth(4)); label(&quot;$30^{\\circ}$&quot;,E,6*(1,0),fontsize(8)); label(&quot;$30^{\\circ}$&quot;,E,7*dir(-32),fontsize(8)); label(&quot;$30^{\\circ}$&quot;,A,9*dir(-56),red+fontsize(8)); label(&quot;$30^{\\circ}$&quot;,A,9*dir(-84),red+fontsize(8)); label(&quot;$3$&quot;,1.1*midpoint(A--B),red); label(&quot;$8$&quot;,0.4*midpoint(A--D),red); [/asy]\" width=\"325\" height=\"335\" />\nNote that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/5/f75d6d58b03031bd7cb52a7ca886a8ddf369d21c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/a/b2a6812a4e2f0371eff84427f0b74bef0280159a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAD = 60^{\\circ}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"114\" height=\"15\" /> Applying the law of cosines, we get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee7af4fb55d74e0520644bdec71439ed9da5d91.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} BD^2 &amp;= AB^2+AD^2-2AB\\cdot AD \\cdot\\cos{60^{\\circ}} \\\\ &amp;= 9 + 64 - 2 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 8 \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ &amp;= 49, \\end{align*}\" width=\"322\" height=\"89\" />\nfrom which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/c/fcc19356c9a3ee4a32e4b60550773980534e12d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD = 7.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"70\" height=\"14\" /> \n</p><p>From here, we wish to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/e/f4eaf2dc3a215ea9f2e436369c8806e1296ad8a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BF.$\" width=\"30\" height=\"12\" /> As <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/d/c9daba06f5ec9c5069f24bbeab9c7151ab4f68c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> is the angle bisector of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/2/232ed26750e4e4f5f3b14faedab47c2b9c6a32eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAD,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"64\" height=\"18\" /> we apply the angle bisector theorem:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/2/8a2e33124f70e54c0b8d2fa45bf08fc6d284e757.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\frac{AB}{BF} &amp;= \\frac{AD}{DF} \\\\ \\frac{3}{BF} &amp;= \\frac{8}{7-BF}. \\end{align*}\" width=\"123\" height=\"81\" />\nSolving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/8/668de69306cec703cef80a6dc7758ad406e63845.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BF,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"31\" height=\"16\" /> we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/4/7e4f177594816cd9c88fa44e5562213ac81033f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BF = \\frac{21}{11}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"82\" height=\"38\" /> Remember to scale the figure back up by a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/8/2f885f96d2fb7e65f800de4ff71d7dcd0a5d2db5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"13\" height=\"16\" /> so our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/1/541381587ccb5695adb70aca3855e1afaf6bdaf1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{21}{11}\\cdot 3 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(E) } \\frac{63}{11}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"143\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p>~lprado ~MRENTHUSIASM\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Note\">Note</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Note\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Instead of taking the angle bisectors, one could also take area. The area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/9/1e94f1abd32d37d04a5b77e333689bf70ef83864.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DAB$\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/7/8772d61f5af0b70f355caf61084162db9b47f34b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/f/77fa429516dcd46dc87b58002a7cf120a61e3aa1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AF = s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"62\" height=\"14\" /> and so through area formulae <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/d/d5df5a0e1760bb26d6b15e42ff14f823fbbac0e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2s + \\frac{3s}{4} = \\frac{11s}{4} = 6\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"176\" height=\"38\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/2/232a04e94085b9e0d4190059c7fdb49b92318fab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s = \\frac{24\\sqrt{3}}{11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"81\" height=\"43\" />. Through the law of cosines, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/8/ff822d7e1e01ef84d5b409f2aa002e2a9eac451e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BF = \\frac{21}{11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"77\" height=\"38\" /> so scaled we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/a/78a155bee32dc78e2acc0bd526e392bcb0007c8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{63}{11}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"29\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_Law_of_.28Co.29Sine\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_Law_of_(Co)Sine\">Solution 2 Law of (Co)Sine</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 Law of (Co)Sine\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>From cyclic quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/9/5999e40b162a45a3270b37aad4473cb75eaa4036.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CDAE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/5/da53eb7f1ec11c431d27c21583f09fa2e9e09b2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CAD = \\angle CED = 30^\\circ.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"195\" height=\"15\" /> Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/4/124bf443dc6ea7c2746eb66958f1c1ec8fd845bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABDE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is also cyclic, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/b/cdba9608183372269dd1052bf50b9614bb3beb8b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAD = \\angle BED = 60^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"190\" height=\"15\" />, so, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/2/112100d0ee920f56e26b776da9fd6f3a66a4433b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle BAC= \\angle BAD - \\angle CAD = 60^\\circ - 30^\\circ = 30^\\circ.\\]\" width=\"366\" height=\"13\" />\nUsing Law of Cosines on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/5/f75d6d58b03031bd7cb52a7ca886a8ddf369d21c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/5/cd5085a7209e5db8f1327ea9285bbe397c7a5181.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[BD^2=9^2+24^2-2(9)(24)\\cos(60^\\circ).\\]\" width=\"283\" height=\"20\" /> Solving, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/e/d6e0e86f8cfdf9891271a55aea68e39a16a93467.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD=21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"75\" height=\"14\" />. Next, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/5/5f53e621e4de15c3ac04d029b663d34fc0c2b9df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BF}=x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/a/05aa16a2fdfb78e23497f3dcd60170dab4e3bc79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AFB = \\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"91\" height=\"14\" />, which means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/5/4c5ce659d72f730310ff657a07e41ebaa7fa4b62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{FD}=21-x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"107\" height=\"19\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/7/bc782f045addd7580adf260d25f793c2da6c6483.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AFD = 180-\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"141\" height=\"16\" />. Using Law of Sines on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/d/97d59b1384670dfc0b60fb9b4f6610e37e3f8c18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AFB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/e/e0e6873b865b472fbd12b67022ac0db4eb17398d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{9}{\\sin \\theta}=\\frac{x}{\\sin 30}.\\]\" width=\"111\" height=\"37\" /> Solving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/5/865211471c7cc8aff3d88f9f2b843bd262159050.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin \\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"36\" height=\"14\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/a/0caa8cf8f9c7b8b5a17171f8193b7f8779da5376.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin \\theta = \\frac{9}{2x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"84\" height=\"38\" />. Now we apply the Law of Sines to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/b/0bb27abf13f822044f67b854faddb23789d459de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AFD.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" /> We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/a/67ae07d8c3e5dc0d95a05f1c642c525defbff6d6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{24}{\\sin(180-\\theta)} = \\frac{21-x}{\\sin 30}.\\]\" width=\"179\" height=\"41\" /> Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/8/e481f5649823ca464024c6ae54da077aa044a324.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(180-\\theta) = \\sin(\\theta),$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"172\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/a/0caa8cf8f9c7b8b5a17171f8193b7f8779da5376.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin \\theta = \\frac{9}{2x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"84\" height=\"38\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/c/85cde0db494bd5573ae85fbc5ff6f78a5fc9bae7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{16x}{3} = 42-2x.\\]\" width=\"118\" height=\"37\" /> Solving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/a/7fa40e9b54cb06aa92e65036ce124b937622bc8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{x=\\frac{63}{11}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"70\" height=\"49\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/4/93468fc6db12a67507f0d70db3103a9fe9a1dd00.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) } \\frac{63}{11}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"69\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~evanhliu2009\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Ptolemy.E2.80.99s_.2B_Similarity.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Ptolemy’s_+_Similarity)\">Solution 3 (Ptolemy’s + Similarity)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Ptolemy’s + Similarity)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/3/f13a96240c51d61ba3733d9f5c3020fa92ec4136.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCDE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" /> cyclic, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/7/db74d1cb67b48589cbba3cec9c70ed5701639676.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAC=\\angle CAD=\\angle BEC=30^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"268\" height=\"15\" />. Hence cyclic quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/7/a3722b8bc3b8bb1ee9426732ee6f6272d800a7bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAD=60^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"109\" height=\"15\" />. Law of Cosines on triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/5/7e538978649c14e1616fac744e983b5981d0ea8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BAD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/6/506ef054e6e87fe39c41590cf87e97289bf3aafb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BD}^2=9^2+24^2-2\\cdot9\\cdot24\\cos60^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"269\" height=\"23\" />. Hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/e/2ce8e6fd424e29fa884a10169a32dd6bbf72234e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BD}=21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"75\" height=\"18\" />. Since triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/a/d7ada763e99852a6e44a15d46cce3c3709a944d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> is a 120-30-30 triangle, we can use law of sines or just memorize ratios to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/6/c66ebb6ce8e1d6a4a393c5e164b96102fc6db6fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC}=\\overline{CD}=7\\sqrt3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"143\" height=\"21\" />. Now Ptolemy’s on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/6/8f657e29e879cfd6bdd927d0fae41797cddd2f10.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7\\sqrt3(9+24)=21\\overline{AC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"169\" height=\"24\" />. Hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/7/1b763e5d1655479a14e16b602380efd12f217aa0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AC}=11\\sqrt3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"96\" height=\"21\" />. Now notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/1/9611dc8586006b823430cb7304d4d0248bcc9687.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BCF=\\angle ACB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"138\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/9/249609eb551a69fd29d9d5eae3990d82d2bbce68.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CBF=\\angle CAB=30^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"188\" height=\"15\" />. Hence triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/5/d454ccad55388ce38766e919a448421c4633323a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CBF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/9/459b39e026037707282c95dfdbfd6dc64c855a16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CAB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> are similar, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/a/8baff559fe9b629759e96d9bf99b8da5a75e3301.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\overline{BF}}{\\overline{BC}}=\\frac{\\overline{AB}}{\\overline{AC}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"91\" height=\"44\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/5/df5e6626c84265612381fcbe481b4fc0c74e635f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\overline{BF}}{7\\sqrt3}=\\frac9{11\\sqrt3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"110\" height=\"47\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/6/8d6bf79a4e6a435f438f6231ec6be53490151926.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BF}=\\frac{63}{11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"77\" height=\"38\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/4/93468fc6db12a67507f0d70db3103a9fe9a1dd00.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) } \\frac{63}{11}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"69\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~benjamintontungtungtungsahur (look guys im famous)\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Area_.26_Angle_Bisector_Length.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Area_&amp;_Angle_Bisector_Length)\">Solution 4 (Area &amp; Angle Bisector Length)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Area &amp; Angle Bisector Length)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>As shown in previous solutions, the angles subtending the same arcs give us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/3/f03ba61c0089ba3ffc1dc440dcfcf6b30d37448c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAC = \\angle BEC = 30^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"188\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/5/da53eb7f1ec11c431d27c21583f09fa2e9e09b2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CAD = \\angle CED = 30^\\circ.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"195\" height=\"15\" /> This tells us that \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/7/067eb05d9053ce47f45a1eef4c0e315cf96ebac5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle BAD = \\angle BAC + \\angle CAD = 60^\\circ,\\]\" width=\"268\" height=\"16\" />\nand line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/d/c9daba06f5ec9c5069f24bbeab9c7151ab4f68c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> acts as the interior angle bisector of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/c/d4ce625f543e6bc2e57b21c563b09bafec558f7c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAD.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>We can find the length of the angle bisector <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/d/c9daba06f5ec9c5069f24bbeab9c7151ab4f68c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> by splitting the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/5/f75d6d58b03031bd7cb52a7ca886a8ddf369d21c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" /> into the sum of the areas of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/7/1b7ee1894b9868699832ce22d92598b8f0b8997a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABF$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/8/328703d8157a5761b4ff513fb0165c991d1d9781.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AFD$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/b/49b7894c8af4f10a52c53336ebf36b48bf5d8d5d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\text{Area}(\\triangle ABD) = \\text{Area}(\\triangle ABF) + \\text{Area}(\\triangle AFD).\\]\" width=\"374\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Using the sine formula for area (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/0/0203ca34d108501c4a808999d0091df9c0126324.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2}ab\\sin C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"134\" height=\"38\" />), we have:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/1/9615d0a6f0f41faa6de41c726d845ce92ba5051c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{2}(AB \\cdot AD) \\sin 60^\\circ = \\frac{1}{2}(AB \\cdot AF) \\sin 30^\\circ + \\frac{1}{2}(AD \\cdot AF) \\sin 30^\\circ.\\]\" width=\"502\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Substituting the known values <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/f/a9fe059ea3506a79afe2df3583a0b5e584fb92d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/6/ca6371efb1262af8539ffffcb75a931ef3fb43cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD = 24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/812cff33ea4bcfb3948ad15c22c4a9dbdec1ae44.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{2}(9 \\cdot 24) \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} = \\frac{1}{2}(9 \\cdot AF) \\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{1}{2}(24 \\cdot AF) \\frac{1}{2}.\\]\" width=\"333\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>Multiplying the entire equation by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to clear the denominators yields:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/8/d280c250b194c9737f0d1f94190df32d02cf5886.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} 216\\sqrt{3} &amp;= 9(AF) + 24(AF) \\\\ 216\\sqrt{3} &amp;= 33(AF) \\\\ AF &amp;= \\frac{216\\sqrt{3}}{33} = \\frac{72\\sqrt{3}}{11}. \\end{align*}\" width=\"207\" height=\"100\" />\n</p><p>Now, we apply the Law of Cosines on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/7/1b7ee1894b9868699832ce22d92598b8f0b8997a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABF$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> to solve directly for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/e/65e4f2d5cc59e5ffbed3734130e8c45b643adc91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d3b439b22ad2ef9095d0763aab02cb04645d71.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[BF^2 = AB^2 + AF^2 - 2(AB \\cdot AF)\\cos 30^\\circ.\\]\" width=\"328\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Substituting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/e/c8e1863ac1a60aad1474a87b0dc1ec49d27ce472.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = 9,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"18\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/348f5c32f51c8c72a07df66cef8ef33803dcbaf9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AF = \\frac{72\\sqrt{3}}{11},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"105\" height=\"43\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/c/e9ce626f2d9d70976980ca81e2e67a9fc7eae64e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos 30^\\circ = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"107\" height=\"43\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/2/e028fc7c4de9fdca34c7e37d984ff6fe020dc655.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} BF^2 &amp;= 9^2 + \\left(\\frac{72\\sqrt{3}}{11}\\right)^2 - 2 \\cdot 9 \\cdot \\frac{72\\sqrt{3}}{11} \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\ BF^2 &amp;= 81 + \\frac{15552}{121} - \\frac{1944}{11}. \\end{align*}\" width=\"333\" height=\"100\" />\n</p><p>Finding a common denominator of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/a/76ad7692f5d86be790209a56a68c2a3488235054.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$121$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/4/1d44474bc61274501bff50f1fc3054ce14f56184.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} BF^2 &amp;= \\frac{81 \\cdot 121 + 15552 - 1944 \\cdot 11}{121} \\\\ BF^2 &amp;= \\frac{9801 + 15552 - 21384}{121} \\\\ BF^2 &amp;= \\frac{3969}{121}. \\end{align*}\" width=\"278\" height=\"124\" />\n</p><p>Taking the square root of both sides (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/b/efbe1e33ddf689cf6ed2bc572a6e262af2ecf1fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{3969} = 63$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"96\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/1/1b1a08b1da43b26aeeab00348d4cd770b03f4982.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{121} = 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"87\" height=\"21\" />), we find:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/b/36b6a91da5308c03e51bbebd23df942ceb61417c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[BF = \\frac{63}{11}.\\]\" width=\"78\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Thus, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/c/04c23f862e4bb76b0918ec8e6cd3a1101b1c6bba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) } \\frac{63}{11}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"74\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p>~ARJUNKHOKHAR\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Power_Solve\">Video Solution by Power Solve</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Power Solve\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/Vd_kvodRjNQ?si=ZuoUjGLXcZter8PB&amp;t=753\">https://youtu.be/Vd_kvodRjNQ?si=ZuoUjGLXcZter8PB&amp;t=753</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28Cyclic_Quads_.2B_LoC.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(Cyclic_Quads_+_LoC)\">Video Solution (Cyclic Quads + LoC)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (Cyclic Quads + LoC)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/tlre7Nxt1HY?si=LujdKSJ7atb-3Cke\">https://youtu.be/tlre7Nxt1HY?si=LujdKSJ7atb-3Cke</a> - Continuum Math\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_4_by_SpreadTheMathLove\">Video Solution 4 by SpreadTheMathLove</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><s